{"title":"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45e3d817886b4d9dbd6bb74ad23463ed139ed68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/1951589baea0f3a9ef308cbd84601f6fd3f4f008.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} P(0) = P(3) = \\cdots &amp;=&amp; P(3n) = 2, \\\\ P(1) = P(4) = \\cdots &amp;=&amp; P(3n-2) = 1, \\\\ P(2) = P(5) = \\cdots &amp;=&amp; P(3n-1) = 0, \\quad\\text{ and }\\\\ &amp;&amp; P(3n+1) = 730.\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"361\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p>Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Lagrange Interpolation Formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b81ffbf6d572d963cea024bd59f9a80e7cb210b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 2\\sum_{p=0}^{n}\\left ( \\prod_{0\\leq r\\neq3p\\leq 3n}^{{}}\\frac{x-r}{3p-r} \\right )+ \\sum_{p=1}^{n}\\left ( \\prod_{0\\leq r\\neq3p-2\\leq 3n}^{{}} \\frac{x-r}{3p-2-r}\\right )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"509\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c002a0727119afe985b348c789dda9209658e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+1) = 2\\sum_{p=0}^{n}\\left ( \\prod_{0\\leq r\\neq3p\\leq 3n}^{{}}\\frac{3n+1-r}{3p-r} \\right )+ \\sum_{p=1}^{n}\\left ( \\prod_{0\\leq r\\neq3p-2\\leq 3n}^{{}} \\frac{3n+1-r}{3p-2-r}\\right )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"585\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>after some calculations we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cf7b1147842ffa50ed482d26b6d3d29c81cb23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+1) =\\left ( \\binom{3n+1}{0}- \\binom{3n+1}{3}+\\binom{3n+1}{6}- ... \\right )\\left ( 2.(-1)^{3n}-1 \\right )+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"597\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aad4262a3405384dfc025443f7ec79fa4bdef75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+1)= 730$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> so we have to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/c/9fc358016692a4564a5d429a49f4a73d85e3a0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left ( \\binom{3n+1}{0}- \\binom{3n+1}{3}+\\binom{3n+1}{6}- ... \\right )\\left ( 2.(-1)^{3n}-1 \\right )= 729$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"517\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Lemma: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is even  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd0c96cf4e109cf5b5fd8bb79f0f88e3b99585b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{p}{0}- \\binom{p}{3}+ \\binom{p}{6}- \\cdots = \\frac{2^{p+1}sin^{p}\\left ( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right )(i)^{p}\\left ( cos\\left ( \\frac{p\\pi}{3} \\right ) \\right )}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"438\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>and if  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is odd  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02ce7ec3e6ad914176103922183a1154cf729043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{p}{0}- \\binom{p}{3}+ \\binom{p}{6}- \\cdots = \\frac{-2^{p+1}sin^{p}\\left ( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right )(i)^{p+1}\\left ( sin\\left ( \\frac{p\\pi}{3} \\right ) \\right )}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"470\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfeb75fb36b8987924cd73c3c30c75435bd3b4ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\nUsing above lemmas we do not get any solution when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, but when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/8531383cde1c8db278fcf98bcaa0d975a16099bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n+1=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies the required condition, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IGn9u1au5pE\">Video Solution</a> by Olympiad frameworks</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The (3n+1)th differences of the polynomial are zero. Call it p(x), so we have p(3n+1) - (3n+1)C1 p(3n) + (3n+1)C2 p(3n-1) - ... + (-1)3n+1 p(0) = 0, where rCs is the binomial coefficient. Hence p(3n+1) = 2( (3n+1)C1 - (3n+1)C4 + ... ) + ( (3n+1)C3 - (3n+1)C6 + ... ). Putting n = 1, we get: p(4) = 2( 4C1 - 4C4) + 4C3 = 6 + 4 = 10. So n is not 1. Putting n = 2, we get: p(7) = 2( 7C1 - 7C4 + 7C7) + ( 7C3 - 7C6) = 2( 7 - 35 + 1) + (35 - 7) = -26. So n is not 2. Putting n = 3, we get: p(10) = 2( 10C1 - 10C4 + 10C7 - 10C10) + ( 10C3 - 10C6 + 10C9) = 2(10 - 210 + 120 - 1) + (120 - 210 + 10) = -162 -100 = -262. So n is not 3. Putting n = 4, we get: p(13) = 2( 13C1 - 13C4 + 13C7 - 13C10 + 13C13) + ( 13C3 - 13C6 + 13C9 - 13C12) = 2(13 - 715 + 1716 - 286 + 1) + (286 - 1716 + 715 - 13) = 1458 - 728 = 730. So n = 4 works.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO\" title=\"1984 USAMO\">1984 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017115257\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 145/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1237/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest e